/span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">d</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">p₁ </span><span class=\"fn\">p₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.dvd_bmod_coeffs_cert\">dvd_bmod_coeffs_cert</a> <span class=\"fn\">d</span> <span class=\"fn\">p₁</span> <span class=\"fn\">p₂</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">d</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Dvd.dvd\">∣</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Poly.denote'\">Poly.denote'</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">p₁</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\">d</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Dvd.dvd\">∣</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Poly.denote'\">Poly.denote'</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">p₂</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`d ∣ p₁` implies `d ∣ a * p₁`, and the coefficients of the latter can be reduced modulo `d`.\nThe solver uses `a = 1`, or the inverse of the leading coefficient of `p₁` modulo `d` when it is\ncoprime to `d`, so that `p₂` is equivalent to `p₁` and its leading coefficient is `±1`.","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.dvd_bmod_coeffs","kind":"theorem","line":1168,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.dvd_bmod_coeffs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Ini